import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Pressleaf Privacy Policy" description="Pressleaf extracts page text and builds Markdown documents on your device. Document folders, which can contain source URLs, saved page content and images, are stored on your device and sync between your iPhone and Mac through your own iCloud. The developer has no access to these folders." lang="en">
  <article>
    <nav aria-label="Language">
      <a href="/pressleaf/privacy/" hreflang="en" lang="en" aria-current="page">English</a>
      <a href="/pressleaf/privacy/ko/" hreflang="ko" lang="ko">한국어</a>
    </nav>

    <h1>Pressleaf Privacy Policy</h1>
    <section>
      <h2>Documents and iCloud</h2>
      <p>Pressleaf extracts page text and builds Markdown documents on your device. Document folders, which can contain source URLs, saved page content and images, are stored on your device and sync between your iPhone and Mac through your own iCloud. The developer has no access to these folders.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Requests to websites</h2>
      <p>When you save a link, Pressleaf may request the page and its images directly from the sites that host them. When saving a public X post, Pressleaf may request it from X using its public post ID. Those sites receive ordinary connection information such as your IP address and apply their own privacy policies.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Wayback Machine</h2>
      <p>If a page is missing and you choose to look for a copy in the Wayback Machine, Pressleaf sends only the source URL as lookup data to the Internet Archive. If you choose to import a result, Pressleaf requests that archived page. The Internet Archive applies its own privacy policy.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Developer access and support</h2>
      <p>The App Store build uses no developer-operated server, analytics, tracking or automatic crash reporting. If you email support, we receive the message and anything you choose to include. We use that information to respond to your request.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Storage and deletion</h2>
      <p>Documents remain in your library until you delete them. To remove saved material, delete the document from Pressleaf and check any copies you exported separately. You can manage iCloud access in system settings. You can request deletion of support correspondence by contacting us.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p><a href="mailto:oozoofrog@oozoofrog.dev">oozoofrog@oozoofrog.dev</a></p>
    </section>
    <footer><a href="/pressleaf/support/">Pressleaf Support</a></footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  article { max-width: 48rem; margin: 0 auto; line-height: 1.65; }
  nav { display: flex; gap: 1rem; }
  section, footer { margin-block: 1.5rem; }
</style>
